  "reason": "All four completed experiments use avgpool aggregation, leaving the aggregation strategy entirely unexplored. The current best (config_025: scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.6776) establishes a strong baseline, and config_014 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding every other setting identical. This isolates whether a learned, attention-based aggregation of multiple profiles captures interactions that simple averaging misses. Given that the RNA encoder choice (scvi vs pca) produced the largest single gain (~4%), the aggregation mechanism is the next most impactful untested dimension in the multiprofile pipeline. The result is informative either way: improvement confirms transformer aggregation is worth pursuing, while a null or negative result confirms avgpool sufficiency and redirects the budget toward fusion strategy or image encoder choice."
}

